ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
- Adding a new module requires only a descriptor (plus role-actions), no new tool code,
  in the common case.
- A citizen token can only see and do what the gateway/access control already allows.
- No call ever accepts agent-supplied user identity, RequestInfo, URL, method or raw body.
- get_payment_link returns a working link and never triggers a payment.
- Every write needs a valid confirmation token bound to the exact payload.
- Correlation ID appears in MCP logs, audit and downstream gateway logs.